 "fix": {
  "title": "Plan 29 Task 6: the screw search without n^4 pair fits (triage proposal 3, ruling P29-7)",
  "mechanism": "symmetry._helical tried every pair of copies as the screw and tested each on every copy against every member of its cluster: n^4/2 pair fits (23FR's 42 copies: 1.26 million _Assembly.pair calls). A fit's RMSD is at least the distance between the moved and the target centroids of its matched atoms, so a member whose centroid lands farther than the tolerance (plus 1e-6 \u00c5 for rounding) is passed over unfitted; the first member within the tolerance, in cluster order, is the one the full search took.",
  "named": [
   "23FR"
  ],
  "expected": "23FR's time only; every figure byte-identical"
 },
